# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artifacts and run outputs.
#
# This repo tracks SOURCE and FROZEN TRUTH: code, physics profiles, suite
# declarations, frozen case lists, and the small result jsons. Everything a run
# produces stays out -- it is either regenerable from what is here, or it is a
# multi-hundred-MB blob that does not belong in git history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Ad-hoc backups. Git is the backup; these were the pre-git convention.
*.bak
*.bak_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model checkpoints. 595 MB each, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, and
# training artifacts rather than source. train_eval/ckpt/PROVENANCE.txt records
# the upstream path and sha256 for each -- restore from there before an eval.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.pth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated viewer / rollout pages. Each embeds robot meshes and base64 textures,
# so they run 9-30 MB apiece (1.0 GB in total here). All are rebuildable:
#   viewers      <- tasks/*/pipeline/build_*_viewer*.py  from the tracked npz
#   rollout HTML <- a driver run (render/rollout_viewer.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output directories. Results of past runs, not inputs to future ones.
# The numbers worth keeping live in the tracked summary/report jsons.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/replay_test/
/trial/
/trial_multigpu/
/bench_runs/

# Eval outputs: keep the jsons (the actual measurements, ~3 MB), drop the rest
# (npz frame dumps, logs, ipc fifos).
/train_eval/eval/**/*.npz
/train_eval/eval/**/*.log
/train_eval/eval/**/*.fifo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party dataset assets.
#
# LIBERO object meshes: 130 files, 106 MB, derived from the LIBERO dataset
# (yifengzhu-hf/LIBERO-datasets). Rebuild with
# bench_libero/tasks/libero/pipeline/batch_libero_realmesh.py once the source
# hdf5 files are downloaded. The object TRAJECTORIES (*_flow.npz,
# goal_pointflow.npz) ARE tracked -- they are our extraction, and small.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/pointflow/**/*_mesh.npz
**/libero/samples/
**/libero/pipeline/texture_map.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code belonging to other people, kept locally but not republished from here.
#
# vendor/flow_policy is a frozen copy of a colleague's model implementation
# (see train_eval/ckpt/PROVENANCE.txt for the source path and date), and
# _upstream/ holds reference implementations from the upstream training repo.
# Both are needed to RUN an eval and neither is ours to publish; see README.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/train_eval/vendor/
/_upstream/

# Local scratch
/tmp/
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-investigation suites emitted by tasks/libero/build_env/pick_case.py.
# Each is a throwaway naming a handful of cases; regenerate with
#   pick_case.py --env <env_id> [--match <substr>]
# The declarative suites (libero_object_flow_v1.yaml) ARE tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bench_libero/suites/libero_pick_*.yaml
bench_libero/suites/libero_smoke_*.yaml
bench_libero/suites/libero_one_*.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OBJ sidecars for the LIBERO scene props. Written by
#   build_env/build_object_urdf.py --props
# from the props/*/mesh.npz that ARE tracked, so they are pure derived output:
# 21 MB of ASCII (basket alone is 7.4 MB) reproducible byte for byte in one
# command. The .urdf files next to them ARE tracked -- those carry the mass /
# inertia derivation and the provenance header, which is source, not output.
#
# (envs/*/*.obj were committed in 9f65a61 before this rule existed; they stay,
# rewriting that history is not worth 28 MB.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bench_libero/tasks/libero/props/*/*.obj
